WEBVTT

1
00:02:27.625 --> 00:02:28.745
<i>Sub Inspector Mala, come in.</i>

2
00:02:29.125 --> 00:02:30.309
- Yes, go.
<i>- Diverting the plane.</i>

3
00:02:30.333 --> 00:02:31.375
- Where?
<i>- Gate number 82.</i>

4
00:02:31.458 --> 00:02:32.458
Gate number 82. Let's go.

5
00:02:33.458 --> 00:02:34.833
<i>Control to KL436.</i>

6
00:02:35.042 --> 00:02:37.333
Turn back to the terminal.
You are not clear to take off.

7
00:02:44.417 --> 00:02:45.583
Coming to gate number 82.

8
00:02:46.708 --> 00:02:47.708
<i>Ladies and gentlemen,</i>

9
00:02:47.958 --> 00:02:49.878
<i>as per the latest communication
from the captain,</i>

10
00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:51.768
<i>we regret to inform you
that our flight will be returning</i>

11
00:02:51.792 --> 00:02:53.792
<i>to the terminal
due to some technical difficulties.</i>

12
00:02:54.417 --> 00:02:57.226
<i>We kindly ask that you remain seated
in your assigned seats at this time.</i>

13
00:02:57.250 --> 00:02:59.893
<i>Rest assured, we will keep you updated
as soon as we receive more information.</i>

14
00:02:59.917 --> 00:03:02.208
<i>We apologize
for any inconvenience caused.</i>

15
00:03:02.583 --> 00:03:03.583
<i>Thank you.</i>

16
00:03:11.125 --> 00:03:12.125
Geeta Sethi.

17
00:03:16.625 --> 00:03:17.625
Divya Rana.

18
00:03:22.125 --> 00:03:23.125
Jasmine.

19
00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:27.871
We need you to come with us.

20
00:03:28.542 --> 00:03:30.875
Sir, could you please tell us
what is wrong?

21
00:03:33.542 --> 00:03:35.342
Do you really want me
to spill the beans here?

22
00:03:39.083 --> 00:03:40.083
Let's go.

23
00:03:49.417 --> 00:03:50.875
<i>I'm Divya Rana from Haryana.</i>

24
00:03:51.417 --> 00:03:52.417
<i>Head girl.</i>

25
00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:53.500
<i>State Champion.</i>

26
00:03:53.833 --> 00:03:56.083
<i>PCM average 99.8.</i>

27
00:03:56.458 --> 00:03:57.667
<i>I was famous.</i>

28
00:03:58.083 --> 00:03:59.917
<i>I'm from Haryana, Nanheri.</i>

29
00:04:00.458 --> 00:04:01.899
<i>You probably have never heard of it.</i>

30
00:04:02.208 --> 00:04:03.875
<i>We had this crappy airport</i>

31
00:04:04.292 --> 00:04:05.708
<i>that never saw any planes.</i>

32
00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:09.708
<i>Guess it's where my dreams
of becoming a pilot took off.</i>

33
00:04:18.208 --> 00:04:19.542
Ma'am, hands up.

34
00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:24.417
You seem like a good girl.
When did you switch sides?

35
00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:26.750
<i>In fact, an astrologer made a prediction</i>

36
00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:28.583
<i>that someday I would reach for the skies.</i>

37
00:04:29.208 --> 00:04:30.292
<i>What a fraud!</i>

38
00:04:31.625 --> 00:04:32.809
<i>As soon as my board exams
were done,</i>

39
00:04:32.833 --> 00:04:34.917
<i>we moved to Mumbai.</i>

40
00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:36.625
<i>My dad took a loan,</i>

41
00:04:36.708 --> 00:04:39.125
<i>and he got me into a flying school.</i>

42
00:04:44.583 --> 00:04:46.518
And listen, you just gotta know
her mom's maiden name

43
00:04:46.542 --> 00:04:48.250
and her first dog's name.

44
00:04:48.542 --> 00:04:50.042
- Right.
- What the hell, Chintu!

45
00:04:50.375 --> 00:04:51.695
You're back to selling passwords?

46
00:04:52.042 --> 00:04:53.476
Didn't you learn
from what happened last time?

47
00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:55.208
Please, try to understand.

48
00:04:55.292 --> 00:04:57.667
Ma'am, today's the deadline
for filing GST.

49
00:04:57.750 --> 00:04:59.042
Please send me the bill.

50
00:04:59.125 --> 00:05:00.708
Please, try to understand.

51
00:05:00.792 --> 00:05:02.708
I won't be able
to help you later. Yes.

52
00:05:02.875 --> 00:05:05.250
Just send it over,
and I'll take care of the rest, alright?

53
00:05:06.583 --> 00:05:08.208
It's not like she's going off to war!

54
00:05:08.292 --> 00:05:09.208
Well, at least I'm going somewhere.

55
00:05:09.292 --> 00:05:11.792
Hurry up, or you're going
to miss your flight.

56
00:05:11.875 --> 00:05:14.958
How can she miss it
when the pilot is right here?

57
00:05:15.042 --> 00:05:17.833
<i>How do I tell them that their
dear Divya Rana is also a fraud?</i>

58
00:05:18.708 --> 00:05:20.917
<i>As soon as I graduated,
the economy crashed.</i>

59
00:05:21.292 --> 00:05:22.125
<i>Eventually, I found a job,</i>

60
00:05:22.208 --> 00:05:24.049
<i>not in the front of the plane,
but in the back.</i>

61
00:05:24.375 --> 00:05:26.792
<i>I didn't have the courage
to break my family's heart.</i>

62
00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:29.417
<i>A lie is a dangerous thing.</i>

63
00:05:29.542 --> 00:05:31.875
<i>To hide one,
you have to tell a hundred more.</i>

64
00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:38.750
Take it off.

65
00:05:39.958 --> 00:05:40.958
What now?

66
00:05:41.625 --> 00:05:42.625
Shoes.

67
00:05:51.958 --> 00:05:53.917
Twenty years in the airline business.

68
00:05:54.958 --> 00:05:57.250
Consider this an end
to your career and reputation.

69
00:05:59.417 --> 00:06:02.375
<i>You can choose to play fair,
but life always has a twist planned.</i>

70
00:06:03.208 --> 00:06:06.250
<i>Mr. Sethi and I both came
from well-to-do families.</i>

71
00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:08.951
<i>But then came the huge fight
between the Sethi brothers,</i>

72
00:06:09.125 --> 00:06:12.167
<i>and we had to leave our palace
and go into exile.</i>

73
00:06:12.833 --> 00:06:15.208
<i>I easily got a position as an air hostess.</i>

74
00:06:15.333 --> 00:06:18.333
<i>I was Miss Karnal '98, you see.</i>

75
00:06:18.417 --> 00:06:20.250
Oh wow, Mrs. Sethi.

76
00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:22.250
You're looking really hot today.

77
00:06:23.375 --> 00:06:24.375
Say it for me, will you?

78
00:06:24.792 --> 00:06:27.000
- What?
- The jazz… two doors in the front,

79
00:06:27.083 --> 00:06:28.643
two in the back,
and oxygen in the middle?

80
00:06:28.667 --> 00:06:29.875
No, Arun.

81
00:06:29.958 --> 00:06:31.500
Come on, please.

82
00:06:36.875 --> 00:06:39.417
If the air pressure
in the cabin drops,

83
00:06:39.833 --> 00:06:43.708
the oxygen masks above your seats

84
00:06:44.083 --> 00:06:46.792
will drop down automatically.

85
00:06:47.208 --> 00:06:48.208
Are you sure?

86
00:06:48.375 --> 00:06:49.958
Stay seated,

87
00:06:50.625 --> 00:06:52.208
pull the mask towards you,

88
00:06:52.667 --> 00:06:54.833
cover your nose and mouth,

89
00:06:55.875 --> 00:06:57.500
and breathe normally.

90
00:06:59.375 --> 00:07:01.792
- And?
- For any kind of assistance,

91
00:07:02.417 --> 00:07:05.000
please contact our crew.

92
00:07:08.667 --> 00:07:09.667
I got an order.

93
00:07:10.125 --> 00:07:12.208
Geetu, skip work.

94
00:07:12.333 --> 00:07:13.333
Take a day off.

95
00:07:13.792 --> 00:07:16.312
They haven't paid you any salary
for the past six months anyway.

96
00:07:16.833 --> 00:07:18.583
You keep making "contact" for nothing.

97
00:07:21.333 --> 00:07:23.083
I don't feel like going either.

98
00:07:23.458 --> 00:07:24.851
But how can I miss out
on the daily allowance

99
00:07:24.875 --> 00:07:26.195
we get for international flights?

100
00:07:26.292 --> 00:07:28.333
We're surviving on butter chicken
and naan anyway.

101
00:07:28.792 --> 00:07:30.333
I'm just waiting

102
00:07:30.667 --> 00:07:33.833
for the bloody airplane
to hand me my Provident Fund,

103
00:07:34.333 --> 00:07:36.625
so we can move to Goa
and start our own restaurant.

104
00:07:39.208 --> 00:07:40.667
Hello, Brother-in-law!

105
00:07:43.375 --> 00:07:47.083
Geetu, suitcase… Punnu's here.

106
00:07:49.917 --> 00:07:52.000
Hey, Punnu? Sapna?

107
00:07:52.083 --> 00:07:53.125
Surprise!

108
00:07:53.500 --> 00:07:55.417
Happy Diwali, Geetu.

109
00:07:56.917 --> 00:07:58.417
Happy Diwali…

110
00:08:00.167 --> 00:08:01.167
Greetings.

111
00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:12.809
Forget Diwali, it looks like they'll be
here for Holi with all that luggage.

112
00:08:12.833 --> 00:08:14.417
Look at Sapna's face.

113
00:08:15.125 --> 00:08:16.486
I bet they fought with each other.

114
00:08:17.625 --> 00:08:18.750
It's my fault.

115
00:08:19.667 --> 00:08:22.042
I couldn't take care
of him after Mom passed away.

116
00:08:22.125 --> 00:08:23.125
That's true.

117
00:08:26.750 --> 00:08:28.042
Don't get too emotional.

118
00:08:28.458 --> 00:08:29.500
You're not his mother.

119
00:08:30.250 --> 00:08:32.333
"I couldn't take care
of him after Mom passed away."

120
00:08:32.708 --> 00:08:33.768
As if he would've become
the Prime Minister of India

121
00:08:33.792 --> 00:08:34.792
if your mom were alive.

122
00:08:36.583 --> 00:08:38.000
<i>We middle-class people</i>

123
00:08:38.167 --> 00:08:40.917
<i>have to grind all day
to make ends meet.</i>

124
00:08:41.875 --> 00:08:45.167
<i>I didn't even realize when I went
from being a beauty queen to a maid.</i>

125
00:08:56.750 --> 00:08:57.958
You have expensive taste.

126
00:09:00.875 --> 00:09:01.875
Hands up.

127
00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:08.750
You are definitely doing time in jail.

128
00:09:10.375 --> 00:09:11.625
<i>As my grandpa would say,</i>

129
00:09:12.250 --> 00:09:13.410
<i>"Told you this would happen!"</i>

130
00:09:18.083 --> 00:09:19.083
You witch!

131
00:09:21.708 --> 00:09:22.976
Indulging in debauchery, are we?

132
00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:24.042
Who the hell are you?

133
00:09:24.542 --> 00:09:25.458
Where is that dog?

134
00:09:25.542 --> 00:09:27.726
- Where's my bloody husband?
- Hey, I didn't cheat on you.

135
00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:29.667
Anshul!

136
00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:30.917
<i>I should've freaking known.</i>

137
00:09:31.333 --> 00:09:33.853
<i>These guys in Presidential Suites
always turn out to be married.</i>

138
00:09:34.833 --> 00:09:35.833
Anshul!

139
00:09:37.083 --> 00:09:37.917
Anshul!

140
00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:39.480
Babe, this is not what it looks like.

141
00:09:39.542 --> 00:09:41.059
- Please, please, I can explain.
- I'm going to kill.

142
00:09:41.083 --> 00:09:42.083
Give me a chance, okay?

143
00:09:42.542 --> 00:09:43.742
I'm going to kill you, bloody…

144
00:09:44.375 --> 00:09:45.875
- You're hurting me!
- Let me go.

145
00:09:45.958 --> 00:09:47.125
Babe, let's not overreact.

146
00:09:47.208 --> 00:09:48.792
I'm sorry. Let me explain.

147
00:09:50.458 --> 00:09:51.833
Leave me!

148
00:09:52.417 --> 00:09:56.042
- I made a mistake. I'm sorry.
- Is this a mistake you're sorry for?

149
00:09:56.208 --> 00:09:57.208
I…

150
00:10:00.542 --> 00:10:02.875
<i>My parents were madly
in love when they got married.</i>

151
00:10:03.208 --> 00:10:04.449
<i>But love alone is never enough.</i>

152
00:10:04.667 --> 00:10:07.507
<i>Everyone kept saying, "Have a kid,
and everything will fall into place."</i>

153
00:10:07.875 --> 00:10:09.018
<i>But that didn't solve a thing.</i>

154
00:10:09.042 --> 00:10:10.042
<i>And here I am.</i>

155
00:10:11.917 --> 00:10:13.333
<i>Eventually, they got divorced,</i>

156
00:10:13.417 --> 00:10:15.917
<i>and I ended up
in Jabalpur with my grandpa.</i>

157
00:10:18.375 --> 00:10:20.458
<i>Poor Grandpa used to stress over</i>

158
00:10:20.542 --> 00:10:22.583
<i>who would look out for me
once he was gone.</i>

159
00:10:25.083 --> 00:10:27.084
<i>In fact, people always
felt sorry for me, thinking,</i>

160
00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:28.500
<i>"Poor girl."</i>

161
00:10:29.667 --> 00:10:31.333
<i>Do you know who isn't poor though?</i>

162
00:10:32.167 --> 00:10:33.167
<i>The rich folks.</i>

163
00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:37.417
<i>My dreams were always bigger
than Jabalpur and Greenfield School.</i>

164
00:10:38.333 --> 00:10:40.750
<i>I just needed some money
to break free from there.</i>

165
00:10:42.333 --> 00:10:46.833
<i>So, I swiped a math paper
from Mrs. Khullar's locker and sold it.</i>

166
00:10:47.292 --> 00:10:48.542
<i>The headmistress found out.</i>

167
00:10:48.833 --> 00:10:50.476
<i>She gave me a whole bunch
of threats at first,</i>

168
00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:52.375
<i>but then she actually agreed at 30%.</i>

169
00:10:52.875 --> 00:10:54.596
<i>As they say, money makes
the world go round.</i>

170
00:10:56.417 --> 00:10:59.333
<i>I came to Mumbai with dreams and ideas,</i>

171
00:11:00.083 --> 00:11:01.833
<i>but then the reality struck.</i>

172
00:11:02.458 --> 00:11:03.934
<i>I hustled a lot, but sometimes
the supplier wouldn't lend,</i>

173
00:11:03.958 --> 00:11:05.438
<i>and sometimes the buyer wouldn't pay.</i>

174
00:11:08.208 --> 00:11:11.167
<i>And in this hand-to-mouth situation,
I understood two things.</i>

175
00:11:11.917 --> 00:11:15.542
<i>One, you gotta have some money
if you wanna make more.</i>

176
00:11:15.750 --> 00:11:18.292
<i>And two, always have a Plan B.</i>

177
00:11:20.375 --> 00:11:23.500
<i>They say money doesn't bring happiness.</i>

178
00:11:23.917 --> 00:11:26.708
<i>And the ones who are truly happy
ain't rolling in dough.</i>

179
00:11:27.375 --> 00:11:29.256
<i>Guess happiness is just not
in the cards for me,</i>

180
00:11:29.458 --> 00:11:31.000
<i>so if I gotta cry,</i>

181
00:11:31.250 --> 00:11:34.000
<i>I'd rather do it in a Beamer
than in a bloody bus!</i>

182
00:11:37.667 --> 00:11:38.907
Who gave you permission to sit?

183
00:11:41.708 --> 00:11:42.708
Sit.

184
00:11:49.750 --> 00:11:51.833
Section 380A.

185
00:11:53.625 --> 00:11:55.792
Section 380B.

186
00:11:57.208 --> 00:11:58.875
Section 440.

187
00:12:00.917 --> 00:12:03.167
Can anyone guess what this means?

188
00:12:05.042 --> 00:12:06.500
Penitentiary.

189
00:12:09.667 --> 00:12:10.667
Hey…

190
00:12:11.667 --> 00:12:14.750
what's the latest with Kohinoor Airlines?

191
00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:19.708
I want to know.

192
00:12:20.458 --> 00:12:22.917
What was the need to do all this?

193
00:12:23.708 --> 00:12:25.589
BHARTIYA SURAJ
KOHINOOR AIRLINES HEAVILY IN DEBT

194
00:12:30.417 --> 00:12:31.417
Sethi ma'am…

195
00:12:33.375 --> 00:12:34.417
Sethi ma'am!

196
00:12:34.500 --> 00:12:35.500
What?

197
00:12:35.583 --> 00:12:37.064
When will we be getting our salaries?

198
00:12:37.375 --> 00:12:40.055
I really need to pay the loan installment
by the first of the month!

199
00:12:40.125 --> 00:12:41.125
Any clue about it?

200
00:12:41.583 --> 00:12:43.875
I spoke to HR Manager Mittal.

201
00:12:44.042 --> 00:12:47.542
He said everything will be cleared
next week, along with the Diwali bonus

202
00:12:47.708 --> 00:12:48.708
for sure.

203
00:12:49.750 --> 00:12:51.792
You're so sweet, Geetu.

204
00:12:52.333 --> 00:12:54.875
Come on, we won't even get crumbs
for a Diwali treat,

205
00:12:55.458 --> 00:12:57.375
and you're expecting a bonus?

206
00:12:57.875 --> 00:12:59.500
Guts.

207
00:13:00.250 --> 00:13:01.500
<i>Komal, 58.</i>

208
00:13:01.583 --> 00:13:02.583
Thank you, sir.

209
00:13:04.708 --> 00:13:06.708
Divya, 62.5.

210
00:13:07.042 --> 00:13:08.167
Thank you, Mr. Rajvanshi.

211
00:13:10.417 --> 00:13:11.417
Sheetal.

212
00:13:12.958 --> 00:13:14.667
72.5 kilogram!

213
00:13:15.375 --> 00:13:16.375
Oh, God!

214
00:13:16.417 --> 00:13:17.583
We'll have to ground her.

215
00:13:25.583 --> 00:13:26.625
She's unfit to fly.

216
00:13:27.333 --> 00:13:28.333
Yes, sir.

217
00:13:28.958 --> 00:13:29.958
Unfit.

218
00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:39.542
<i>Hello, this is Vijay Walia,</i>

219
00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:41.292
<i>Chairman of Kohinoor Airlines.</i>

220
00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:43.542
<i>Welcome to the Kohinoor family!</i>

221
00:13:44.458 --> 00:13:46.708
<i>Our amazing five-star airline,</i>

222
00:13:46.875 --> 00:13:48.583
<i>where we treat our guests like gods,</i>

223
00:13:49.042 --> 00:13:50.500
<i>is here to serve you.</i>

224
00:13:51.333 --> 00:13:52.167
<i>Kohinoor Airlines is committed to</i>

225
00:13:52.250 --> 00:13:54.101
<i>- providing convenience to its passengers.</i>
- I paid 20,000 for the ticket.

226
00:13:54.125 --> 00:13:55.768
Sir, I understand that you
have paid for your ticket,

227
00:13:55.792 --> 00:13:58.208
but I'm really sorry,
the blankets are finished.

228
00:13:58.292 --> 00:14:00.042
However, let me check again for you.

229
00:14:00.125 --> 00:14:01.125
Just give me a moment.

230
00:14:04.333 --> 00:14:05.333
Mrs. Geeta!

231
00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:08.125
Captain Wadhera!

232
00:14:08.417 --> 00:14:09.875
What a pleasant surprise.

233
00:14:11.292 --> 00:14:13.309
I thought you'd forget all about us
commercial staff

234
00:14:13.333 --> 00:14:15.333
now that you're the private pilot
for the chairman.

235
00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:18.417
How can anyone ever forget you?

236
00:14:20.167 --> 00:14:21.875
- Can I get a...
- Whiskey on the rocks?

237
00:14:25.125 --> 00:14:26.125
I'll get you a coffee.

238
00:14:28.833 --> 00:14:30.042
Oh, Mrs. Geeta,

239
00:14:30.500 --> 00:14:32.260
looks like your boyfriend
is our pilot today.

240
00:14:32.750 --> 00:14:35.311
5A is pressing the call button
like a maniac. Go and handle that.

241
00:14:35.667 --> 00:14:37.000
"Boyfriend," yeah, right!

242
00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:40.875
<i>Voice like a symphony</i>

243
00:14:42.292 --> 00:14:45.625
<i>Eyes so bewitching</i>

244
00:14:45.708 --> 00:14:48.000
<i>Every time you smile</i>

245
00:14:48.708 --> 00:14:51.458
<i>And say what up, O tormentor!</i>

246
00:14:54.375 --> 00:14:57.042
