377
00:20:45.917 --> 00:20:48.125
<i>Ladies and gentlemen,
this is your captain speaking.</i>

378
00:20:48.375 --> 00:20:50.851
<i>Due to a medical emergency, we're heading
back to Mumbai International.</i>

379
00:20:50.875 --> 00:20:52.083
Oh, for God's sake, Divya!

380
00:20:52.625 --> 00:20:54.667
I wasn't this upset,
even at my mom's funeral.

381
00:20:55.292 --> 00:20:58.333
You know, I've never actually seen
a dead body before.

382
00:20:58.625 --> 00:21:00.667
Well, he's always been like
a dead body anyway.

383
00:21:01.208 --> 00:21:02.750
"Mrs. Sethi, my blood pressure is low.

384
00:21:02.917 --> 00:21:04.375
Can you please tally the sales?

385
00:21:04.500 --> 00:21:05.917
Mrs. Sethi, my blood sugar is high.

386
00:21:06.000 --> 00:21:07.321
Can you please upload the meals?"

387
00:21:07.833 --> 00:21:09.625
He never even carried his own bag.

388
00:21:10.875 --> 00:21:12.809
Probably because he's always got
so much gold with him.

389
00:21:12.833 --> 00:21:14.958
Damn. Respect.

390
00:21:21.000 --> 00:21:22.000
Should we keep them?

391
00:21:24.167 --> 00:21:25.167
Where is it?

392
00:21:26.250 --> 00:21:29.083
First, tell us
what you're looking for, ma'am.

393
00:21:29.375 --> 00:21:31.417
No need to act smart!

394
00:21:31.833 --> 00:21:33.875
Where is the gold? Where is it?!

395
00:21:33.958 --> 00:21:35.542
- Gold?
- Gold?

396
00:21:35.625 --> 00:21:36.625
Gold?

397
00:21:38.208 --> 00:21:41.875
Ma'am, we know nothing about the gold!

398
00:21:41.958 --> 00:21:43.792
Do you take me for a fool?

399
00:21:43.875 --> 00:21:46.458
Three months ago,
you found that old man's dead body

400
00:21:46.542 --> 00:21:48.382
who had that vest
with the gold strapped on it?

401
00:21:48.458 --> 00:21:50.375
- Did you or did you not?
- We did.

402
00:21:50.500 --> 00:21:53.125
Don't deny that you
are not working with him.

403
00:21:54.292 --> 00:21:57.000
You, miss? Are you, or are you not?

404
00:22:04.417 --> 00:22:07.167
I have hustled my entire life
to find an investor for my business.

405
00:22:08.625 --> 00:22:10.833
And look, I finally found one.

406
00:22:12.708 --> 00:22:13.917
Sorry, sir. No offense.

407
00:22:15.083 --> 00:22:15.917
Come on, guys.

408
00:22:16.000 --> 00:22:18.375
We've been serving meals
for the past six months

409
00:22:18.917 --> 00:22:20.357
without getting paid a single rupee!

410
00:22:22.167 --> 00:22:23.750
Divya, imagine.

411
00:22:24.250 --> 00:22:25.250
Your loan…

412
00:22:26.250 --> 00:22:28.125
- gone.
- Have you lost your freaking mind?

413
00:22:28.667 --> 00:22:29.893
If we get caught,
we'll not only be banned

414
00:22:29.917 --> 00:22:30.934
from the airlines
but also from the airport!

415
00:22:30.958 --> 00:22:31.958
Idiot!

416
00:22:32.083 --> 00:22:33.083
Geetu.

417
00:22:33.208 --> 00:22:35.458
For years, you've dreamed
of owning a restaurant.

418
00:22:36.625 --> 00:22:38.875
Now, when the money is coming your way,

419
00:22:39.333 --> 00:22:40.625
you are being moralistic.

420
00:22:40.708 --> 00:22:44.458
Look, I didn't spend half
my life as a slave to end up

421
00:22:44.542 --> 00:22:46.375
in prison with you for the remaining half.

422
00:22:46.792 --> 00:22:47.792
Got it?

423
00:22:50.208 --> 00:22:51.208
Fine.

424
00:22:52.417 --> 00:22:53.542
Each to her own then.

425
00:23:02.292 --> 00:23:03.292
Hey!

426
00:23:03.333 --> 00:23:04.333
Don't touch!

427
00:23:04.708 --> 00:23:06.625
And keep quiet.
Don't say another word.

428
00:23:07.667 --> 00:23:09.333
Not to us or to him.

429
00:23:09.625 --> 00:23:10.986
<i>All crew. We're ready for landing.</i>

430
00:23:22.583 --> 00:23:23.583
Hey!

431
00:23:26.875 --> 00:23:29.018
Sir, the oldie was all covered in gold,
just like a new bride!

432
00:23:29.042 --> 00:23:30.042
Tell me about it!

433
00:23:30.625 --> 00:23:33.083
Uncle was being naughty
with one leg already in the grave.

434
00:23:34.333 --> 00:23:36.875
Sir, they found the body.

435
00:23:47.292 --> 00:23:48.292
Hi.

436
00:23:50.667 --> 00:23:51.750
You know him or what?

437
00:23:55.625 --> 00:23:56.625
Somewhat.

438
00:23:57.250 --> 00:23:58.250
Hey!

439
00:23:59.375 --> 00:24:01.042
It's her fault!
She pushed me!

440
00:24:30.875 --> 00:24:32.750
Divya Rana from Haryana.

441
00:24:33.333 --> 00:24:34.500
Jaiveer.

442
00:24:35.792 --> 00:24:36.792
Air hostess?

443
00:24:38.417 --> 00:24:40.083
I never thought we would meet again!

444
00:24:41.625 --> 00:24:43.375
- And you...
- Customs.

445
00:24:44.042 --> 00:24:45.167
Customs!

446
00:24:45.458 --> 00:24:47.139
Yes, I actually just got transferred here.

447
00:24:47.208 --> 00:24:50.089
If I had known I'd meet you here,
I would've asked for a transfer sooner.

448
00:24:50.375 --> 00:24:53.292
Ma'am, could you please sign here
and here?

449
00:24:53.375 --> 00:24:54.375
Okay.

450
00:24:55.167 --> 00:24:56.727
And, also write down your phone number.

451
00:24:57.167 --> 00:24:59.327
I might need to call you again
for further questioning.

452
00:25:00.125 --> 00:25:00.958
- Oh.
- Sir,

453
00:25:01.042 --> 00:25:02.351
the representatives
from the airline are here.

454
00:25:02.375 --> 00:25:03.500
Fine, I'll talk to them.

455
00:25:03.750 --> 00:25:04.833
- Can I go now?
- Sure.

456
00:25:04.917 --> 00:25:05.917
Thank you.

457
00:25:06.792 --> 00:25:08.125
- See you later?
- See you.

458
00:25:08.208 --> 00:25:10.143
Looks like we'll be bumping
into each other quite often now.

459
00:25:10.167 --> 00:25:11.167
Yeah.

460
00:25:11.625 --> 00:25:12.708
Are you happy now, sir?

461
00:25:13.167 --> 00:25:14.792
He's an employee of your airline, right?

462
00:25:15.833 --> 00:25:17.643
Is this what your airline
is resorting to nowadays?

463
00:25:17.667 --> 00:25:20.750
- He was carrying 12 kilos of gold!
- Mr. Mittal.

464
00:25:20.833 --> 00:25:22.914
- Is this how the airline operates now?
- Mr. Mittal.

465
00:25:23.917 --> 00:25:26.037
I'm talking to you, sir.
Are you even listening to me?

466
00:25:30.625 --> 00:25:31.625
How much does it weigh?

467
00:25:32.125 --> 00:25:33.125
Twelve kilos.

468
00:25:34.917 --> 00:25:36.125
And where was he coming from?

469
00:25:36.542 --> 00:25:37.982
He wasn't coming, sir. He was going.

470
00:25:38.667 --> 00:25:40.167
- Where?
- Al Burj.

471
00:25:41.667 --> 00:25:43.208
- Keep an eye on them.
- Yes.

472
00:25:46.667 --> 00:25:47.667
Rajvanshi?

473
00:25:48.875 --> 00:25:50.292
Our Rajvanshi? That codger?

474
00:25:51.500 --> 00:25:53.417
I still can't believe that old man,

475
00:25:54.083 --> 00:25:56.417
almost at death's door,
was smuggling gold.

476
00:25:56.792 --> 00:25:57.917
Money, Geetu.

477
00:25:59.000 --> 00:26:00.000
Money.

478
00:26:01.000 --> 00:26:03.351
It can make even the most upright folks
turn into gangsters.

479
00:26:03.375 --> 00:26:06.458
Maybe we were too naive all our lives,
that's why we're unsuccessful.

480
00:26:08.917 --> 00:26:10.083
Geetu, sometimes, I feel…

481
00:26:12.458 --> 00:26:15.167
I couldn't do enough for you.

482
00:26:24.375 --> 00:26:25.417
Seriously.

483
00:26:26.458 --> 00:26:28.099
What you did was more than enough for me.

484
00:26:28.750 --> 00:26:30.958
<i>Grandpa, your bookie is a thief.</i>

485
00:26:31.042 --> 00:26:33.333
Grandpa, why don't you stick

486
00:26:33.417 --> 00:26:34.851
to playing Bingo
like the other old folks?

487
00:26:34.875 --> 00:26:37.667
Hey, you were supposed
to come back after two days.

488
00:26:37.750 --> 00:26:38.917
Long story.

489
00:26:39.333 --> 00:26:40.375
Hey, Mr. Deshmukh!

490
00:26:41.000 --> 00:26:42.875
- What brings you here?
- Jasmine.

491
00:26:43.125 --> 00:26:44.125
Jasmine.

492
00:26:45.708 --> 00:26:48.500
You haven't paid the rent
for the last six months.

493
00:26:49.083 --> 00:26:52.125
The water bills, gas bills,
and society dues are also…

494
00:26:53.833 --> 00:26:55.250
Happy Diwali, Mr. Deshmukh!

495
00:26:59.958 --> 00:27:00.958
You sold the car?

496
00:27:01.583 --> 00:27:02.958
Your flight was canceled?

497
00:27:03.042 --> 00:27:04.083
Why did you sell the car?

498
00:27:06.167 --> 00:27:08.458
Well, we hardly ever use it anyway.

499
00:27:08.542 --> 00:27:10.167
We don't really need a car.

500
00:27:10.458 --> 00:27:12.375
Dad, but that loan belongs to me.

501
00:27:15.250 --> 00:27:16.250
And who do you belong to?

502
00:27:42.750 --> 00:27:45.875
AZAD VEGETABLE MARKET

503
00:27:45.958 --> 00:27:48.792
I only have a few dollars left.
You gave me a good rate, right?

504
00:27:53.583 --> 00:27:55.625
- Sudha.
- Geetu.

505
00:27:55.958 --> 00:27:57.667
- How are you?
- I am okay.

506
00:27:58.000 --> 00:28:00.080
Where is Mr. Mittal?
Doesn't answer my calls anymore.

507
00:28:01.042 --> 00:28:02.842
Sadly, doesn't answer
his wife's calls either.

508
00:28:03.958 --> 00:28:05.768
Remember when I was still
an air hostess in Kohinoor,

509
00:28:05.792 --> 00:28:06.875
he would hover all over me…

510
00:28:08.208 --> 00:28:09.458
like a bug.

511
00:28:09.542 --> 00:28:10.768
Now, I can't get my hands on him.

512
00:28:10.792 --> 00:28:11.917
Like a bug?

513
00:28:12.667 --> 00:28:13.708
Right. Yeah.

514
00:28:14.458 --> 00:28:15.375
Good one.

515
00:28:15.458 --> 00:28:17.292
- See you.
- Gourd... Okay.

516
00:28:17.375 --> 00:28:18.875
- How much for the gourd?
- 300 rupees.

517
00:28:18.958 --> 00:28:20.958
Are the gourds studded with diamonds?

518
00:28:34.125 --> 00:28:37.708
Three airline companies
have shut down in the last ten years.

519
00:28:38.208 --> 00:28:43.542
And now your airline company
is going to default on a loan.

520
00:28:43.625 --> 00:28:46.167
Look, these things are common in business.

521
00:28:46.458 --> 00:28:48.583
We are a family of 4,000 members.

522
00:28:48.875 --> 00:28:49.875
A small family.

523
00:28:50.708 --> 00:28:52.208
I give my word

524
00:28:52.625 --> 00:28:54.250
to the banks, the government,

525
00:28:54.917 --> 00:28:57.083
and millions of Indians

526
00:28:57.417 --> 00:28:59.792
who entrusted us
with their precious faith.

527
00:29:01.417 --> 00:29:02.917
You don't have to worry.

528
00:29:03.833 --> 00:29:05.417
Even after ten years,

529
00:29:05.875 --> 00:29:07.292
we will still be here.

530
00:29:08.542 --> 00:29:09.667
We are Kohinoor.

531
00:29:10.083 --> 00:29:12.875
We'll always shine. In India.

532
00:29:13.792 --> 00:29:15.059
- Thank you, Mr. Walia.
- Thank you.

533
00:29:15.083 --> 00:29:19.125
<i>Borrowing money to splurge
is not beneficial for any businessman.</i>

534
00:29:19.250 --> 00:29:21.625
<i>He may have to pay a heavy price for it.</i>

535
00:29:21.708 --> 00:29:22.958
These are just speculations.

536
00:29:23.125 --> 00:29:24.250
It's utter nonsense.

537
00:29:24.375 --> 00:29:25.809
- None of our flights have been canceled.
- Sir…

538
00:29:25.833 --> 00:29:26.833
Get out.

539
00:29:27.083 --> 00:29:28.643
Find out who is spreading these rumors!

540
00:29:28.833 --> 00:29:29.875
We will sue them!

541
00:29:47.083 --> 00:29:48.417
Hey!

542
00:29:55.042 --> 00:29:56.042
Mr. Mittal.

543
00:29:58.125 --> 00:30:00.667
You, your wife Sudha, and I…
we go way back.

544
00:30:01.208 --> 00:30:02.792
I consider you like my big brother.

545
00:30:03.833 --> 00:30:05.874
Can I ask you something?
Will you be honest with me?

546
00:30:07.917 --> 00:30:11.042
Is it true that our company is bankrupt?

547
00:30:11.125 --> 00:30:12.917
What are you saying, ma'am?

548
00:30:13.333 --> 00:30:14.809
Don't tell me you've started
believing the rumors as well.

549
00:30:14.833 --> 00:30:17.083
- Our company is the second best in Asia.
- Sir…

550
00:30:17.167 --> 00:30:19.292
- We just leased six airbuses.
- Mr. Mittal,

551
00:30:19.375 --> 00:30:21.667
- for God's sake, the truth.
- Okay, yes, it's bankrupt.

552
00:30:21.750 --> 00:30:23.000
I swear to God, it's bankrupt.

553
00:30:25.292 --> 00:30:26.892
I'm not sure why I shared that with you.

554
00:30:27.417 --> 00:30:29.417
But please, don't tell anyone,
not even by mistake.

555
00:30:30.167 --> 00:30:31.208
It would cause a riot.

556
00:30:31.292 --> 00:30:35.792
So… my Provident Fund?

557
00:30:36.250 --> 00:30:37.250
Will I ever get it?

558
00:30:37.292 --> 00:30:40.792
I'm not saying
that the Provident Fund is lost.

559
00:30:41.083 --> 00:30:42.917
But you know how the system works, right?

560
00:30:43.167 --> 00:30:45.625
If not us, our children will
definitely receive the money.

561
00:31:05.708 --> 00:31:07.083
Sethi ma'am, this is the last box.

562
00:31:07.250 --> 00:31:10.625
Alright, now let's quickly grab
all the peanut packets.

563
00:31:11.208 --> 00:31:14.042
What are we going to do with the peanuts?

564
00:31:14.417 --> 00:31:17.958
- We'll sell them at the traffic signals!
- Okay.

565
00:31:28.583 --> 00:31:29.750
Jasmine. Very good.

566
00:31:29.833 --> 00:31:32.793
Grab a garbage bag from over there
and start collecting all the headphones.

567
00:31:35.500 --> 00:31:37.708
She has been popping anxiety pills
since morning.

568
00:31:39.000 --> 00:31:40.292
I don't think it's working.

569
00:31:45.042 --> 00:31:46.042
Geetu…

570
00:32:05.083 --> 00:32:06.958
God works in mysterious ways.

571
00:32:08.542 --> 00:32:10.142
Yesterday, we were reaching for the sky,

572
00:32:10.750 --> 00:32:12.550
and now we've crashed back down
to the ground.

573
00:32:15.333 --> 00:32:16.333
For two decades,

574
00:32:17.000 --> 00:32:18.792
I worked my butt off like a maid.

575
00:32:19.333 --> 00:32:22.958
We let them deduct taxes

576
00:32:24.167 --> 00:32:25.476
and the Provident Fund every month.

577
00:32:25.500 --> 00:32:26.917
We let them screw us over.

578
00:32:28.333 --> 00:32:30.042
I had such big plans.

579
00:32:31.917 --> 00:32:34.250
Arun and I were going
to start a restaurant in Goa…

580
00:32:36.083 --> 00:32:37.708
and enjoy our second honeymoon.

581
00:32:38.083 --> 00:32:41.458
I don't know how
to break it to my parents…

582
00:32:43.042 --> 00:32:45.833
that the pilot uniform they adore so much

583
00:32:46.833 --> 00:32:50.167
is actually a rental.

584
00:32:53.417 --> 00:32:56.542
Imagine if we had
Rajvanshi's gold with us.

585
00:32:57.792 --> 00:33:00.000
Seriously, we should've taken it
for ourselves.

586
00:33:01.417 --> 00:33:03.792
Actually, <i>we </i>lost our freaking minds,
not you.

587
00:33:04.333 --> 00:33:05.167
Sorry.

588
00:33:05.250 --> 00:33:09.042
I wonder how long that bloody
Rajvanshi has been doing this.

589
00:33:09.125 --> 00:33:10.792
Four years, three months, and

590
00:33:11.042 --> 00:33:12.042
twenty-one days.

591
00:33:15.750 --> 00:33:16.750
What's this?

592
00:33:17.333 --> 00:33:18.333
Plan B.

593
00:33:31.458 --> 00:33:32.458
What?

594
00:33:32.750 --> 00:33:34.167
It's not like he really needed it.

595
00:33:34.833 --> 00:33:37.917
Anyway, this is Rajvanshi's roster.

596
00:33:38.208 --> 00:33:40.250
All the flights are to Al Burj.

597
00:33:40.792 --> 00:33:44.375
He always messaged
this number once he arrived there.

598
00:33:46.417 --> 00:33:48.875
Let's see who this rascal

599
00:33:48.958 --> 00:33:50.184
- was messaging all the time.
- Sethi ma'am,

600
00:33:50.208 --> 00:33:52.059
it's getting late.
Let's wait and do this tomorrow.

601
00:33:52.083 --> 00:33:54.208
I've waited enough! Give it to me.

602
00:34:00.333 --> 00:34:01.333
Hello?

603
00:34:01.792 --> 00:34:02.792
Who's this?

604
00:34:03.042 --> 00:34:04.167
It's me.

605
00:34:06.792 --> 00:34:09.101
Sudha, how many times have
I told you not to touch my things?!

606
00:34:09.125 --> 00:34:11.250
<i>Why are women calling you
this late at night?</i>

607
00:34:12.917 --> 00:34:14.208
Hello? Wrong number!

608
00:34:15.542 --> 00:34:17.750
That old fellow Rajvanshi who died,
his partner…

609
00:34:18.125 --> 00:34:19.125
Manoj Mittal.

610
00:34:20.083 --> 00:34:21.404
Don't pretend you don't know him.

611
00:34:21.542 --> 00:34:24.708
We do. He's the HR head
at Kohinoor Airways.

612
00:34:26.292 --> 00:34:28.875
The HR head or also the head of your gang?

613
00:34:29.750 --> 00:34:30.667
Gang?

614
00:34:30.750 --> 00:34:31.750
Gang?

615
00:34:32.083 --> 00:34:34.292
No. He is a nice guy.

616
00:34:35.083 --> 00:34:36.083
Like you?

617
00:34:37.667 --> 00:34:40.750
Okay. You tell me, how did you do it?

618
00:34:48.917 --> 00:34:51.333
- Hello, Mr. Mittal.
- Hello to you too!

619
00:34:52.042 --> 00:34:53.250
Oh, ma'am, it's you!

620
00:34:53.708 --> 00:34:54.708
Not fair, Mr. Mittal.

621
00:34:55.208 --> 00:34:58.792
We can't afford plain biscuits
while you are feasting on gold biscuits?

622
00:34:59.125 --> 00:35:01.565
Well, Mr. Mittal, I must say,
you've got a sneaky side to you.

623
00:35:02.750 --> 00:35:04.625
I don't understand.

624
00:35:05.500 --> 00:35:09.250
We also don't understand
what to do with this phone.

625
00:35:10.000 --> 00:35:11.292
Oh…

626
00:35:11.583 --> 00:35:13.333
Thank God!

627
00:35:13.750 --> 00:35:15.042
And thank you.

628
00:35:15.458 --> 00:35:16.750
This phone was with you guys?

629
00:35:17.375 --> 00:35:19.083
That's great. Please give it back.

630
00:35:19.458 --> 00:35:20.333
What can I say?

631
00:35:20.417 --> 00:35:22.737
We all have to do something
to support our families, right?

632
00:35:23.708 --> 00:35:25.549
Then help us support
our families as well, sir.

633
00:35:26.000 --> 00:35:27.000
What do you mean?

634
00:35:27.042 --> 00:35:29.667
We can do what Mr. Rajvanshi
used to do, three times over.

635
00:35:38.208 --> 00:35:39.569
Look, this isn't something chicks…

636
00:35:39.833 --> 00:35:42.875
I mean, "ladies" should be doing.

637
00:35:42.958 --> 00:35:44.208
Please, excuse me.

638
00:35:45.208 --> 00:35:46.249
You were saying something?

639
00:35:46.792 --> 00:35:47.875
Look, Mr. Mittal,

640
00:35:48.125 --> 00:35:50.417
we "ladies" aren't making a request,

641
00:35:50.625 --> 00:35:51.826
we're giving you an ultimatum.

642
00:35:52.042 --> 00:35:53.958
Either you team up with us willingly,

643
00:35:54.167 --> 00:35:56.875
or we'll turn you over to customs.
Choose.

644
00:35:56.958 --> 00:35:58.083
- Let me go, please.
- Geetu?

645
00:35:59.542 --> 00:36:00.625
Hi, Geetu.

646
00:36:01.042 --> 00:36:02.042
Mrs. Sudha!

647
00:36:02.667 --> 00:36:05.625
Hey, Geetu, why don't I see you anymore?
Why did you quit the gym?

648
00:36:05.708 --> 00:36:08.292
- I was strapped for cash.
- Oh.

649
00:36:09.000 --> 00:36:10.841
But I don't think
that'll be a problem anymore.

650
00:36:11.417 --> 00:36:15.167
- Right, Mr. Mittal?
- Yes, of course.

651
00:36:18.917 --> 00:36:19.917
The crew.

652
00:36:22.042 --> 00:36:23.833
This one or this one?

653
00:36:24.167 --> 00:36:25.458
- Take both.
- You sure?

654
00:36:26.958 --> 00:36:28.875
- Bye, Geetu.
- Bye.

655
00:36:31.875 --> 00:36:33.208
See you tomorrow.

656
00:36:47.583 --> 00:36:49.000
<i>Hey, girl!</i>

657
00:37:04.125 --> 00:37:05.725
You guys will be able to do this, right?

658
00:37:06.958 --> 00:37:08.833
No, I mean, since it's your first time…

659
00:37:10.792 --> 00:37:13.672
People often think about running away
with it when it's their first time.

660
00:37:14.792 --> 00:37:15.792
Don't run away.

661
00:37:16.917 --> 00:37:18.477
Because I don't just have your address,

662
00:37:19.167 --> 00:37:20.958
I have your entire personal history.

663
00:37:22.250 --> 00:37:23.708
When you reach the airport there,

664
00:37:24.083 --> 00:37:26.708
